Kirstie Alley's final TV role was an  unexpected one but that was all part of  her plan here's how she surprised the  world one last time in a bulky pink  Mammoth costume  Kirstie Alley kept working almost right  up until her sudden surprising death at  age 71. some of the actresses late  career projects had been television  series including scream queens and  flaked and movies such as accidental  love and you can't take my daughter her  final television appearance though came  in April 2022 on The Masked Singer she  did make one public appearance on camera  after that but not on TV roughly three  months before her death on December 5th  2022 Ali shot a promo letting fans know  she was joining The Cameo app where fans  can pay to request personalized video  messages she deployed her classic  deadpan humor showing she was the same  performer she'd always been giving  examples of possible messages people  could send hi I love you or  um you know Merry Christmas or I want a  divorce whatever you need I'll deliver  Ali showed that same willingness to  please as baby mammoth on the seventh  season of The Masked Singer she was  introduced in her costume singing  walking after midnight by Patsy Cline  she later sang the Shoop Shoop song it's  in his Kiss by Cher and me too by Meghan  Trainor Ali was eliminated in The  Season's eighth week the judges had  difficulty recognizing who was behind  the mask earlier in the season the only  one to correctly guess her was Jenny  McCarthy Ali said her prior relationship  with McCarthy made her think she would  correctly guess who she was in her exit  interview Ali described the difficulties  of wearing her baby mammoth costume  which included a giant cartoonish pink  head the cheers star joked that she may  have chosen a different costume if she  could go back in time describing the  disguise as constricting and nearly  blinding she advised future performers  when you're choosing your costumes go  skimpy according to deadline the  producers of The Masked Singer announced  after her passing that the show would  pay respect to the actress with a  tribute card airing during its special  holiday episode while Ali kept plenty  busy with work toward the end of her  life she explained after her Masked  Singer appearance that the show was  something new for her a shake-up to her  life and career about 10 years ago I  realized I always had to keep mixing my  career mixing my life up or it was going  to get really mundane she said she also  did the show to please a specific  audience her grandchildren she told Los  Angeles Times I have grandchildren and  they're really young so they are going  to think this is good the actress never  held back when gushing about her  grandchildren in public including in  2017 when she couldn't say enough good  things about spending the holidays with  her grandson Ali told people when I got  up in the morning as soon as that baby  was up I was holding that baby traipsing  around with him and showing him all the  Christmas lights and singing to him  foreign
 

